<title>UK: C&amp;W Jamaican unit's year profits rise.</title>
<headline>C&amp;W Jamaican unit's year profits rise.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Cable and Wireless Plc said on Monday that net profit after tax at its subsidiary Telecommunications of Jamaica Ltd (TOJ) had risen 41 percent over the last year.</p>
<p>TOJ's profit after tax for the year to March 31, 1997 rose to J$2.67 billion, or around 48 million stg. Operating revenues at TOJ increased to JS11.48 billion from J$9.75 billion.</p>
<p>Cable &amp; Wireless owns 79 percent of TOJ, which provides local and international telephone, telegraph and telex services in Jamaica.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 4019</p>
